WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:05.759
SCP Foundation agents stationed at Area 37
had intercepted chatter from a normally closed

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:08.170
communication system in a nearby city.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.280
To anyone else, the calls that the Foundation
were eavesdropping would seem innocent - even

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.080
boring, but the Foundation immediately recognized
the coded language being used.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.260
They were listening to communications between
underground cells of The Serpent’s Hand

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:28.100
- a dangerous paramilitary organization that
stands in opposition to everything the Foundation

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.800
is trying to do.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.960
Once deciphered, the Serpent’s Hand messages
revealed plans for killing Foundation personnel,

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:40.210
breaking into containment sites, and releasing
anomalous creatures and objects into the world

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:45.350
- pretty standard stuff for the Foundation’s
least-favorite, anomaly-loving insurgents.

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:50.060
But they kept using one code that even the
Foundation didn’t have any intel on - they

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.010
kept asking about the condition of The Sisters.

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.879
Fate has a funny way of sneaking up on you
though, and in time, they would know more

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:04.180
about the powerful, sadistic, reality-warping
beings known as The Sisters than they could

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:05.479
have possibly imagined.

00:01:05.479 --> 00:01:10.509
But what they would eventually learn was not
the kind of data that anyone would ever want

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:11.680
to have.

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.790
After intercepting clear lines of communication
from a local Serpent’s Hand cell, triangulating

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:21.509
the location of their compound was child’s
play, and Mobile Task Forces were dispatched

00:01:21.509 --> 00:01:26.490
from Area 37 with orders to neutralize the
potential threat before they could mount an

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.560
attack on a facility.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.039
Just when the Serpent’s Hands least expected
it, they had heavily-armed Foundation soldiers

00:01:33.039 --> 00:01:38.310
kicking down their doors, crashing through
windows, and rappelling down from the ceiling.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.900
As expected, the Serpent’s Hand put up a
fight, but thanks to their superior training

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:48.169
and the element of surprise, the Foundation’s
Mobile Task Forces came out on top.

00:01:48.169 --> 00:01:51.940
They were able to capture fifteen surviving
members of the group for interrogation, as

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:55.680
well as a collection of anomalous objects
being stored by the group.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:00.319
Among them were a small wooden loom, an enamel
needle, and a glass eye.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:05.289
When the task force obtained these seemingly
mundane items, a haunted-looking Serpent’s

00:02:05.289 --> 00:02:07.299
Hand began laughing wildly.

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:12.420
He kept repeating, “You have no idea what
you’re getting yourselves into...”

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.480
Nobody knew just how right this man was.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.500
Not yet, anyway.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.310
Congratulating themselves on a job well done,
the Mobile Task Forces hauled their captives

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.590
and the new anomalous items back to Area 37
- a heavily isolated Foundation site that

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:33.070
specializes in the early containment of anomalous
objects for initial observation and study.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:37.230
The objects hadn’t displayed any anomalous
properties in transit - maybe the Serpent’s

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:42.370
Hand was lying and these weren’t dangerous
items at all, or it was actually just a pile

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.370
of junk.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:48.010
Either way, they were sent to a Foundation
researcher on site to conduct preliminary

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:49.010
tests.

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:53.480
The loom, the needle, and the glass eye were
laid out across the table for observation,

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.820
when suddenly, the attending researcher felt
a dark presence looming behind him.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:04.300
He turned, with sweat beading on his brow,
and saw three humanoid, translucent figures

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.560
floating in the air behind him.

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:13.000
They would soon become known as SCP - 1765
One, Two, and Three.

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:17.330
The researcher could feel the power emanating
from these silhouettes - reality seemed to

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:22.680
bend and shimmer around them, the way heat
distorts the air into a mirage.

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:26.450
He could tell right away that they were powerful
reality-warpers.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:30.940
Even in their brief time communicating with
the researcher, One, Two, and Three displayed

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:34.270
both intelligence and unique personalities.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.480
One was clearly the ringleader - displaying
an articulate command of language.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:44.580
Two displayed a more mischievous side, speaking
with a cockney accent and had a tendency towards

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.040
creepy giggling.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:50.770
Three was the least communicative of them
all - preferring to speak in short, simple

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:54.370
sentences, often consisting of just single
words.

00:03:54.370 --> 00:03:59.520
Though of course, actions speak far louder
than words - and it didn’t take long for

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:02.959
the Sisters to define themselves with their
actions.

00:04:02.959 --> 00:04:07.500
One told the scared and confused researcher
that they’d been observing the SCP Foundation

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:11.910
for quite some time, and that they deeply
admired the Foundation’s adherence to the

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:13.470
scientific method.

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:17.329
Of course, the researcher wasn’t so much
“flattered” by the Sister’s statement

00:04:17.329 --> 00:04:20.310
as they were “afraid for their life.”

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:24.300
They tried to call security for backup, but
found that their tongue was withering and

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:27.840
turning into a shrivelled, blackened husk
in their mouth.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.710
The Sisters didn’t like to be interrupted.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:34.990
As the tongueless researcher slowly collapsed
in front of them, the Sisters explained the

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:39.590
purpose of their visit - They wished to assist
the Foundation in their quest for knowledge,

00:04:39.590 --> 00:04:44.129
and, as such, they would conduct a number
of experiments on their behalf.

00:04:44.129 --> 00:04:48.909
They would then happily share the resulting
data with the Foundation to compare notes.

00:04:48.909 --> 00:04:54.349
One expressed optimism, saying that she believed
they were about to embark on a beautiful scientific

00:04:54.349 --> 00:04:55.439
relationship.

00:04:55.439 --> 00:04:58.699
The reality couldn’t be further from the
truth.

00:04:58.699 --> 00:05:03.360
The Sisters began their work, moving rapidly
around the facility, bending and twisting

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.319
reality wherever they went.

00:05:05.319 --> 00:05:10.210
They circled Area 37, marking it as separate
from the rest of the world it inhabited.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:15.729
Area 37 no longer belonged to planet earth
- it belonged to the Sisters.

00:05:15.729 --> 00:05:21.169
It was their private experimentation lab,
filled with live and unwilling guinea pigs.

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:26.699
The Foundation attempted to retake the facility
by force, sending Mobile Task Force Iota-6,

00:05:26.699 --> 00:05:31.470
also known as the Canvas Cats, into the belly
of the beast, but they never returned.

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:36.039
In addition to changing the fabric of reality
itself, they also altered the physical structure

00:05:36.039 --> 00:05:39.749
of Area 37 to better serve their experimental
designs.

00:05:39.749 --> 00:05:47.949
It was divided into four sections, marked
A, B, C, and D, each with its own unique purpose.

00:05:47.949 --> 00:05:53.569
Section A - which had formerly been Area 37’s
storekeeping, mess hall, and dormitories - had

00:05:53.569 --> 00:05:56.930
been the least affected by the Sisters’
attacks on reality.

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:01.449
The biggest alterations were the appearance
of two large, metal vats situated in the east

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:06.680
corner of the mess hall, a monitoring station
connected to other sections of Area 37 that

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:11.870
replaced the storekeeping zones, and an imposing
marble sign hanging above the dormitories

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:13.900
that reads “CONTROL GROUP.”

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:18.690
A quick refresher from science class, the
control group in an experiment is the group

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:23.189
that isn’t subjected to the experimental
effect the others are, so they can be used

00:06:23.189 --> 00:06:25.379
as a benchmark to measure against.

00:06:25.379 --> 00:06:30.229
The same was true here - the prisoners in
the control group were the safest of all,

00:06:30.229 --> 00:06:35.069
but they were forced to do something almost
as bad, they had to watch the horrors playing

00:06:35.069 --> 00:06:37.350
out across the rest of the facility.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:41.210
One of the Sisters would occasionally return
to this section to oversee the feeding of

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:46.439
the control subjects, and to encourage them
to take part in the observation of their unlucky

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.509
peers.

00:06:47.509 --> 00:06:52.379
Section B - which had formerly been Area 37’s
outer grounds and sports facilities - had

00:06:52.379 --> 00:06:56.999
been transformed into the center of a localized
spatial-temporal abnormality.

00:06:56.999 --> 00:07:02.430
In layman’s terms, this meant that its size,
climate, atmospheric composition, pressure,

00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:06.970
and temporal flow were all subject to constant
changes based on the whims of Sister Number

00:07:06.970 --> 00:07:11.340
One - who oversaw all the experiments performed
in Section B.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:18.879
For those unfortunate enough to be trapped
in Section B, SCP-1765-1 was their god.

00:07:18.879 --> 00:07:21.379
But she didn’t subject them to her whims
randomly.

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:26.909
No, in her own words, the purpose of Section
B was to delve into the effects of repetitive

00:07:26.909 --> 00:07:31.190
action performed under unusual conditions
on the human psyche.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:35.529
For example, one experiment was set up to
test the physical and mental fortitude of

00:07:35.529 --> 00:07:39.539
a Researcher, a Field Agent, and a sanitation
worker.

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:43.569
The trio were confined in a sports center
and ordered to measure the length of every

00:07:43.569 --> 00:07:48.629
single pipe and the angle at which each connected
to others with nothing more than a wrench,

00:07:48.629 --> 00:07:52.439
a ruler, a brown paper pad and a ballpoint
pen.

00:07:52.439 --> 00:07:55.660
The task was an arduous one taking over ten
hours.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:59.759
And as soon as the subjects were done, One
restructured the sports center and ordered

00:07:59.759 --> 00:08:01.839
them to perform the task again.

00:08:01.839 --> 00:08:08.130
The same happened another 459 times before
One finally concluded the experiment, leaving

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:12.129
the subjects with broken bodies and minds
in the aftermath.

00:08:12.129 --> 00:08:16.240
Section C - which had previously been the
facility’s main office block - exhibited

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:21.159
a similar level of anomalous activity to Section
B, except that it was the domain of the more

00:08:21.159 --> 00:08:24.410
sadistic and mischievous Sister Number Two.

00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:29.349
Her main area of scientific interest was studying
group dynamics and interpersonal relationships

00:08:29.349 --> 00:08:34.310
during extreme conditions - very extreme conditions.

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:39.010
For one experiment, the office block had been
transformed into a kind of football stadium,

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:42.470
with the goal posts removed and replaced by
concrete bunkers.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:47.800
The two teams were the captured Serpent Hand
members, and the members of MTF Iota-6, fresh

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.260
off their attempt to retake the site.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:55.150
The two groups were forced into a deadly game
with incomprehensible rules - including rising

00:08:55.150 --> 00:09:00.870
platforms and hooded figures throwing fiery
projectiles into the crowd, trying to incinerate

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:01.930
the players.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:06.310
But victory didn’t lead to safety, as the
winners of the game were crushed to death

00:09:06.310 --> 00:09:09.620
with giant metal hammers, just for the fun
of it.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:15.400
Two didn’t even try to pretend that this
act had a valid scientific justification.

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:20.710
Section D - which had once been the facility’s
high-risk containment area - was now the strangest

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:23.260
and most mysterious section of all.

00:09:23.260 --> 00:09:28.370
Under the charge of the equally peculiar and
enigmatic Sister Number Three, this area appeared

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:32.650
physically unchanged from its state prior
to the arrival of the Sisters.

00:09:32.650 --> 00:09:37.100
Temporally, however, Section D was the most
warped of them all.

00:09:37.100 --> 00:09:42.330
It existed in a kind of temporal bubble, outside
of the rest of our reality’s timeline, giving

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:47.560
Three a frightening amount of control over
all that went on in her domain outside of

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.560
time.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.390
There she was performing the most strange
and incomprehensible experiment of all.

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.620
The subject was the former Site Director of
Area 37.

00:09:55.620 --> 00:10:00.020
He was brought to a table, and asked to choose
between two different flavors of ice cream

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.500
that were presented to him.

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:05.060
Sounds simple enough, so then why is this
the worst of them all?

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:07.670
Because the Site Director is caught in a time
loop.

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:13.080
He’s been choosing between various flavors
of ice cream for over ten thousand hours,

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:14.770
and he doesn’t even seem to know.

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.950
Three’s only comment on the matter?

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:18.950
“Delicious.”

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:23.970
All attempts to liberate the unfortunate inhabitants
of Area 37 have failed miserably.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:29.470
The Sisters don’t appear to operate on any
form of logic or empathy, and thus, cannot

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:30.880
be reasoned with.

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.510
With talks having failed and Mobile Task Force
Iota-6’s attempt to retake the site ending

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:40.440
in disaster, the only solution left was to
create a guarded perimeter around the area,

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:44.970
using technology like the Scranton Reality
Anchor to fight back against any potential

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:46.800
escape by the Sisters.

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.620
The Sisters are potentially so dangerous that
if they ever truly set their minds to leaving,

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:56.310
it’s considered acceptable to detonate the
facility’s on-site nuclear warhead in hopes

00:10:56.310 --> 00:10:58.460
of finally putting a stop to them.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:02.800
In the meantime, the Foundation has built
giant external servers for processing the

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:08.220
vast quantities of research data the Sisters
are constantly sending from their horrifying

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.220
experiments.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:14.260
Sadly for the inhabitants of Area 37, their
grim fate continues to this day.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:19.260
The experiments never stop, and the subjects
of said experiments seem to be condemned to

00:11:19.260 --> 00:11:23.420
the eternal torment of SCP - 1765.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:28.440
In a way, their unwilling sacrifice protects
us all - because if ever the Sisters were

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.430
interested in performing experiments on a
larger sample size…

00:11:32.430 --> 00:11:36.360
Well, all we can do is hope we end up in the
control group.

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:43.030
Now go check out “SCP - 1730 - What happened
to Site-13?” and “SCP - 1730 - Epic Final

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:47.890
Battle at Site-13” for more about the strangest
SCP sites around the world.

